@startuml deployer
' Plain-language view of the installer for a non-technical reader: what each part is FOR and what
' YOU have to type in. Colour = how much input it needs (see legend). Rendered by render-diagrams.sh.
title What the installer is made of — and what <b>you</b> have to provide

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #777777
  roundCorner 14
}
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

legend top left
<b>What the colours mean</b>
<back:#E8F5E9>   </back>  green — same for everyone, you do nothing
<back:#E3F0FB>   </back>  blue — found automatically from your device
<back:#FFF3E0>   </back>  amber — about you: you type this in
<back:#FBE9E7>   </back>  red — the fiddly internet bit
<back:#ECEFF1>   </back>  grey — 🔒 your secrets: stay on your computer, never uploaded
endlegend

package "The SelfPrivacy installer" as D {
  rectangle "<b>The SelfPrivacy app + the installer itself</b>\nYou provide: nothing — it's the same for everyone" as a1 #E8F5E9
  rectangle "<b>Which computer & which disk to use</b>\nYou provide: nothing — it detects your device;\nyou just confirm which disk gets erased" as a2 #E3F0FB
  rectangle "<b>How it gets online (wifi or cable)</b>\nYou provide: your wifi name + password (only if wifi)" as a3 #FFF3E0
  rectangle "<b>Your web address + its security padlock</b>\nYou provide: your web address (e.g. selfprivacy.example.com)" as a4 #FFF3E0
  rectangle "<b>Your admin login + the app's secret key</b>\nYou provide: nothing — made on the device automatically" as a5 #FFF3E0
  rectangle "<b>Keeping the security padlock renewed</b>\nYou provide: a web-address provider (automatic with a normal one)" as a6 #FBE9E7
  rectangle "<b>🔒 Your private secrets</b> (keys · padlock · wifi & app passwords)\nStored ONLY on your computer — never uploaded or shared" as a7 #ECEFF1
  a1 -[hidden]down-> a2
  a2 -[hidden]down-> a3
  a3 -[hidden]down-> a4
  a4 -[hidden]down-> a5
  a5 -[hidden]down-> a6
  a6 -[hidden]down-> a7
}
@enduml
